": {"file_name": "CoverLandscape.png", "id": "487236046744268", "uri": "https://scontent-ord5-3.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/75572754_487236050077601_8348865219296916010_n.png?_nc_cat=106&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=dUwV5eq1yx8Q7kNvwGFJe9E&_nc_oc=Adm9Spm6oamdLUO8lPLUVc4PSvbjnJbjEgJtjSAj8re-9bU15cws_xPuFzv61u89QlY&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-3.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=8&oh=00_Afw8uTtltDbRSquvdL8nDmX7Tu-vilJTagvK7OIQ2gyv_A&oe=69B93D01"}, "display_name": "3D scan of a campus", "keywords": ["photogrammetry", "reconstruction", "360camera", "digitization", "scan"], "long_description": "Move like a pedestrian in a campus, reconstructed from videos taken by a helmet-held 360 camera (Garmin Virb), whose trajectory is about 5.2km long.\n\nRight controller:\n- Rotate on the left or right by using the joystick\n- Update the vertical offset (up or down) by using the joystick\n- Choose a location and teleport to it by using the virtual laser pointer\n- Teleport by using the index trigger only if the laser is green (not red)\n\nLeft controller:\n- Move continuously by using the joystick\n- Switch pannel and map by using the grip/hand trigger\n- If both map and pannel are disabled, switch between rendering modes (texturing or normal colors) by pressing the index trigger\n- The map shows the cloud of mesh vertices and the user location\n- If the pannel is enabled, switch between constrained and unconstrained motions by pressing the index trigger\n- The constrained motion controls your height above the ground\n- The pannel shows information about the 3D model and the selected motion.\n", "short_description": "Move continuously like a pedestrian in a campus, which was computed by photogrammetry from two 2496x2496 videos taken by a helmet-held 360 camera (Garmin Virb) and by biking about 5.2km in the campus des C\u00e9zeaux (in Aubi\u00e8re, France)."}]}, "developer_name": "Maxime Lhuillier", "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://maximelhuillier.fr/", "developer_terms_of_service_url